    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>cotton fibres refined into a fluffy absorbant [Source: Wikidata] | White-to-yellowish seed-hair fibers of several species of the genus Gossypium, native to most subtropical areas of the world; used especially for making textile, cord, padding, rag paper, and for cellulose used for plastic and rayon. [Source: Getty AAT]</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
